# Rover P4 75 four-door saloon, 1949-1959.
#
# The "Auntie" Rover: 4,496 mm long, 1,664 mm wide, 1,600 mm high, 2,819 mm
# wheelbase; 2.1-litre six, three-speed gearbox with overdrive, independent front
# suspension. The 75 was the volume P4 and a company director's car of the 1950s;
# David Bache restyled the tail in 1955. The P4 range ran to 1964.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rover_P4
#
# Colours: Black, Sage Green, Dove Grey and Maroon are documented Rover finishes
# of the period.
#
# Weight: 60 in total (black 20, green 18, grey 12, maroon 10). Section F of the
# gaps doc: early prestige models are representative rather than common, so weight
# stays low.
#
# Speed 135 km/h; comfort 105/340 (line). Class 3.
# Dates: 1949-1964, the tail covering later life on British roads.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rover-p4-75.blend. References:
# citycars/references/rover-p4-75/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
name=RoverP475(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=20
intro_year=1949
intro_month=9
retire_year=1964
retire_month=6
speed=135
class=3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=105
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=340

